H 1000
	\bGAME\B: \h024\ba\Buto\bs\Bave, \ba\Buto\blo\Bad, \bsav\Be, \blo\Bad, \bpl\Bay
	\bBASE\B: \h030\bl\Baunch, \bpa\Brk, \bd\Brive, \bx\Bfer, \bsel\Bl, \bhi\Btch, \bset\Bship
	\bMOVE\B: \h026\bj\Bump, \bpos[r]\B, \brot[r]\B, \bb\Base, \bs\Bystem
	\bSHIP\B: \h038\bcs\Bpd, \bcac\Bc, \ban\Bim, \bgh\Bost, \bgo\Bdmode, \bdrain\B(\bs\Belf/\bt\Bgt), \bkill\B(\bs\Belf/\bt\Bgt)
	\bHUD\B: \h043\bn\Btb, \bsho\Bw, \bz\Boom, (\bun\B)\bma\Brk
	\bPLAYER\B: \bcas\Bh, \bre\Bp, \bshi\Bps, \bmo\Bnkey, \brob\Bot, \btr\Bent, \bcos\Btume, \bv\Boice
    \bMISC\B: \h034\bcom\Bmands, \bcoi\Bn, \bdi\Bce, \bpi\Bng, \bpr\Bint/\bsay\B, \bti\Bme, (\bad\Bd)\bcar\Bgo

	Enter \bhe\Blp \i\btopic\B\I  for further help.

	Commands (and their options) can be abbreviated to a unique prefix. Case is ignored, unless otherwise stated. Commands that search for names will stop at the first match found; \
	append \b*\B, \b**\B or \b*\iN\B\I  to stop at the second, third or \iN \Ith match.\.

H 1001
	\bautosave\B\h103save the Auto Save game
	\bautoload\B\h109load the Auto Save game
	\bsave [\islot \I|\idesc \I]\B\h020save the game
	\bload [\islot \I|\idesc \I]\B\h026load a game
	\bplay \isound \I [\iutf \I]\B\h023play a sound effect

	Only \bsave\Bd games can be \bload\Bed. Slot is a single character and will be listed as "Quick Save \islot\I "; it is converted to upper case and appended to the file name, so \
	not all characters are available. Described games will be listed with a leading space. Games are automatically overwritten.\.

H 1002
	\blaunch\B\h188enter space
	\bpark\B\h211place the ship in storage
	\bdrive [\iship \I]\B\h135get a ship out of storage
	\bxfer [\iship \I]\B\h146transfer equipment and commodities
	\bsell [\iship \I]\B\h151sell a ship in storage
	\bhitch [\ibase \I]\B\h128hitch a ride
	\bsetship \iloadout \I [\iship \I]\B\h020set the current ship

	\iShip  \Iis tested as a prefix of the name. It is optional (except for \bsell\B) if there is only one ship stored on the base, otherwise the ships will be listed. \iBase  \Imay \
	only be omitted if you have ships stored on one other base.\.

H 1003
	\bjump \iz, x, y\B\I\h147move forwards/backwards, right/left, up/down
	\bjump [\iobject\I ]\B\h127move to the (targeted) object
	\bpos [=]\in\I\B\h182set or move to a bookmark
	\bpos =\B\h209list bookmarks
	\bpos copy|clip\B\h131use the clipboard to store/set position
	\bpos[r] [\ix, y, z\I [\i, p, y, r \I]]\B\h020display/set (relative) position (and rotation)
	\brot[r] [\ip, y, r \I]\B\h129display/set (relative) rotation
	\bbase\B\h217display base’s nickname or previous base’s name
	\bbase \ibase \B\I\h152go to a base
	\bsystem [\isystem \I [\iobject\I | \ipos \I[, \irot\I ]]]\B
	\h270jump to a system or display current system’s nickname

	Numbers may be suffixed with \bk\B or \bK\B to multiply by 1000. Individual numbers are optional, defaulting to the current value or \b0\B, as appropriate. There are ten \
	bookmarks, \b1\B to \b9\B, with \b0\B set automatically, prior to any movement. The object, base or system is tested as a nickname first, then as a case sensitive substring of \
	the name (prefix \iobject  \Iwith \b~\B to test nickname). The object must be in the current system. \iSystem  \Imay be \b.\B for the current system; as may \ibase  \Ifor the \
	current or previous (via this command) base.\.

H 1004
	\bcspd [\ispeed \I]\B\h129display/set cruise speed
	\bcacc [\itime \I]\B\h150display/set time to reach cruise speed
	\banim [[>|<]wings|\iscript \I]\B\h020perform an animation
	\bghost\B\h213toggle collision detection
	\bgodmode\B\h174toggle invincibility
    \bdrainself\B\h182drain your shield
    \bdraintgt\B\h192drain the targeted object’s shield
    \bkillself\B\h207destroy your ship
    \bkilltgt\B\h217destroy the targeted ship

	Setting a high cruise speed may require loading a game (in order to also recognize the new maximum speed). \bCspd\B will not work with MultiCruise. The default animation \
	opens/closes the bay doors; \bwings\B is short for \bSc_extend wing\B. The first \banim\B command runs forwards, the second reverses; use \b>\B to explicitly run forwards and \b<\
	\B for backwards. \bGodmode\B takes effect on the next load.\.

H 1005
	\bntb [on|off|sight]\B\h020choose display of \un\Uon-\ut\Uargeted \ub\Urackets
	\bshow\B\h136toggles display of everything on the Nav Map
	\bshow houses\B\h053toggles display of the House labels on the Universe Map
	\bshow paths\B\h071toggles filtering of patrol paths on the Nav Map
	\bzoom [\itime \I]\B\h062display/set time to zoom Nav Map
    (\bun\B)\bmark\B\h099(un)mark the targeted object

	Sight will show the brackets when the mouse moves over the ship. Whilst bases will be shown on the Nav Map (and Contact List), it is still necessary to actually visit them to \
	obtain their info.\.

H 1006
	\bcash [[+|-]\iamount \I]\B\h037display/set (relative) amount of money
	\brep \ifaction \I[\ivalue \I]\B\h041display/set reputation with \ifaction\I
	\brep = [\ifaction \I|\ivalue\I]\B\h020set reputation for all factions
	\brep undo\B\h143restore reputation prior to first use of \b=\B
	\bships\B\h181list all your stored ships
	\bmonkey\B\h154give Trent a monkey’s head
	\brobot\B\h182turn Trent into a robot
	\btrent\B\h188restore original Trent
	\bcostume \icharacter\B\I\h041use \icharacter\I  instead of Trent
	\bvoice\B\h181display the current voice
	\bvoice \ivoice\B\I\h119use \ivoice\I  instead of trent_voice

	Faction is tested as a nickname first, then as a prefix of the short name; Police factions are simply the initial of the House. \iValue\I  is a number between -1 and 1 \
	(inclusive); a percentage; or: \bH\B = -0.9; \bh\B = -0.6; \bnh\B = -0.2; \bn\B = 0; \bnf\B = 0.2; \bf\B = 0.6; & \bF\B = 0.9. Costume changes take effect on the next dock, or \
	just save & load. Female characters will not look right, due to still using the male animations.

	Using any voice other than trent_voice during the campaign missions may result in missing voice dialogs which in turn can cause softlocks. To prevent such issues, voice changes \
	will fail if the campaign is not yet completed. This restriction can be bypassed at your own risk by prepending \ivoice\I  with an exclamation mark (!).\.

H 1007
	\bcommands\B\h204list all available commands
    \bcoin\B\h276flip a coin
    \bdice\B\h275roll a dice
    \bping\B\h274measure the network latency (not really)
    \bprint/say \itext\B\I\h182output \itext\I  to the chat
	\btime\B\h274display the current time
	\b(add)cargo \icargo \I [\iquantity \I]\B\h020add \icargo\I  to cargo hold
	
	Do not add too many unique items to the cargo hold as this can corrupt the save file.
